## What is derived from google/adk-python

All 60 records in `eval_defects.jsonl` (30 `label: positive` + 30 `label:
control`) carry `repo: "google/adk-python"` and store, verbatim, a raw
function/method/class body excerpt from that repository's source (the
`pre_fix_source` field) — confirmed by checking the `repo` field's value
distribution across all 60 records (60/60 = `google/adk-python`, no other
value present).

This repository additionally ships raw evidence backing `METHODOLOGY.md`'s and
`results/*.md`'s claimed numbers, under `benchmark/raw/`:
`llm_detector_results.jsonl` (all 195 raw per-model local-LLM responses),
`frontier_judge_answers.jsonl` (all 60 raw frontier-judge responses),
`blinding_key.jsonl` (the anonymized-ID-to-real-record mapping used to score
the blind judging — every field in it is already disclosed in the clear in
`benchmark/eval_defects.jsonl`; this file exists only to let a reader
reproduce the scoring pipeline, not to disclose anything new), and
`control_verification_log.json` (every zero-touch check run while building
the 30 controls, accepted or not).

`frontier_judge_answers.jsonl` and `METHODOLOGY.md` quote short (single-line)
verbatim code fragments from the same underlying google/adk-python excerpts
inside free-text explanation fields (e.g. `assert not failures`, `if not
invocation_result_samples: continue`) — these are short quotations of the
same already-attributed source, not independent third-party inclusions, and
are likewise covered by this NOTICE.

`llm_detector_results.jsonl`, `blinding_key.jsonl`, and
`control_verification_log.json` do not themselves contain google/adk-python
source excerpts (verified: no `pre_fix_source`/`source` field holding a full
excerpt, and no verbatim multi-line code echoed in any free-text field).

## What this repository's own files add

`README.md`, `METHODOLOGY.md`, `TAXONOMY.md`, `control_verification_log.json`,
`llm_detector_results.jsonl`, `frontier_judge_answers.jsonl`,
`blinding_key.jsonl`, and `scripts/` are original work product of this
benchmark's construction (extraction tooling, detector outputs, adjudication
notes, and analysis) and are not themselves google/adk-python source, except
for the short verbatim fragments noted above.

